{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KgfYid2kVrE1mi4RXnyo2h","type":"tool_result","content":"56:Occasionally you may want to print something that Rich would interpret as markup. You can *escape* a tag by preceding it with a backslash. Here's an example::\n67:The function :func:`~rich.markup.escape` will handle escaping of text for you.\n74:Calling ``greet(\"Will\")`` will print a greeting, but if you were to call ``greet(\"[blink]Gotcha![/blink]\")`` then you will also get blinking text, which may not be desirable. The solution is to escape the arguments::\n76:    from rich.markup import escape\n78:        console.print(f\"Hello {escape(name)}!\")\n111:You can convert a string to styled text by calling :meth:`~rich.text.Text.from_markup`, which returns a :class:`~rich.text.Text` instance you can print or add more styles to."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71745e73-87c7-4d2e-931e-0da4a8abaadd","uuid":"8fa03a4d-94e5-4aac-bb14-b3aadd7db438","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:06:51.423Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"56:Occasionally you may want to print something that Rich would interpret as markup. You can *escape* a tag by preceding it with a backslash. Here's an example::\n67:The function :func:`~rich.markup.escape` will handle escaping of text for you.\n74:Calling ``greet(\"Will\")`` will print a greeting, but if you were to call ``greet(\"[blink]Gotcha![/blink]\")`` then you will also get blinking text, which may not be desirable. The solution is to escape the arguments::\n76:    from rich.markup import escape\n78:        console.print(f\"Hello {escape(name)}!\")\n111:You can convert a string to styled text by calling :meth:`~rich.text.Text.from_markup`, which returns a :class:`~rich.text.Text` instance you can print or add more styles to.","numLines":6,"totalLines":6},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KgfYid2kVrE1mi4RXnyo2h","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
